# The repository had no EOL policy at all: nothing declared here, and
# core.autocrlf unset. A checkout produced by a CRLF-writing tool therefore
# leaves `git status` reporting ~973 files as modified when only their line
# endings differ (211814 insertions == 211814 deletions, no content change).
# See docs/HANDOFF-msorchestrator.md §3-5.
#
# `text=auto` lets git detect text vs binary and store text as LF in the index;
# `eol=lf` checks it back out as LF on every platform, which is what the shell
# scripts, the Python entry points and the WSL tooling all expect.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: byte-for-byte, never normalised or diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.gif binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.ico binary
*.webm binary
*.mp4 binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
